Ladybird exposes the spec’s legacy callback form of getUserMedia() as
navigator.webkitGetUserMedia(), in secure contexts, as Blink does: Its
navigator_media_stream.idl declares webkitGetUserMedia, implemented as
getUserMedia, next to the unprefixed legacy method. Gecko exposes the
method as mozGetUserMedia behind a pref. WebKit has only the unprefixed
one, for the sites that its quirk shouldEnableLegacyGetUserMedia lists.
